 AUDIT B — Root-Cause Validation-Metric Inconsistency
================================================================================

  Phase 4 JSON: val_acc=0.443616, val_roc_auc=0.425541 (all conditions, all reps)
  Variant-3 report: val_acc=0.7321, val_roc_auc=0.8247

  [B1] Evaluation using w_init (Seed 42, ||w||=0.1939):
       acc=0.443616, auc=0.425541, f1=0.480418
       --> Matches Phase 4 JSON exactly: YES

  ROOT CAUSE IDENTIFIED:
  Phase 4 computes val_acc/auc/f1 using w_init (the INITIAL random weights),
  NOT a trained weight vector. The evaluation call in run_ptbxl_phase4.py is:
    z_val = X_val @ w_init  (line ~359-364)
  This was intentional — Phase 4 is a timing benchmark, not a training experiment.
  The initial weights have logits in [-1.23, +0.97] and produce near-random predictions.

  The Variant-3 result (acc=0.7321, auc=0.8247) is from the sklearn plaintext
  LogisticRegression model converged over 2000 iterations — a completely separate run.

  [B2] After 10 plaintext gradient steps (LR=0.05, L2=0.01):
       Deg-3: acc=0.7022, auc=0.7899
       Deg-5: acc=0.7046, auc=0.7909

  AUDIT B STATUS: EXPLAINED — no data error, behaviour is by design

